Z||000000||cardealer||10-11-2001||10:44 AM||||after putting in a new adapter plate on my v8 from archie, i now dont have any power to part of my fuse box. there is no power  to stereo, battery outputs, accesories, but i have power to everything else. blinkers, horn, ect.  where does the power come from to power this part of the fuse box? <BR>any ideas?<BR>thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||10-11-2001||12:10 PM||||check the fusable links above/close to the battery, pull on them gently and see if wire is broken within.  May too have fusable links at starter.||||reg||1
Z||000002||cardealer||10-13-2001||09:36 PM||||on your starter, where the main battery cable goes on the solenoid, how many wires is there supposed to be? i only have the main battery cable on there, but i was thinking that there was another wire that went there as well. (my memory is going fast) i took my old adapter plate off about a month ago and just put the new one on last week. i cant seem to find my problem with not getting power to part of my fuse block?<BR>anyone with some more ideas?<BR>thanks||||reg||5
Z||000003||daved||10-14-2001||10:17 AM||||If your horn works, then fuse block BAT/FUSE & STOP HAZ FUSE section must be o/k, and getting power from junction S206, which means fusible link "A" must be o/k.<BR>If the radio and wiper fuses are not powered, I would suspect the ignition switch.  <BR>Can you narrow the problem down a bit?<BR>I'm using the Haynes schematics for Power Distribution, page 271.  Dave||||reg||1
